request: Add a clear command that removes todos whose completed field is true.

governor turn 1: ask  (The request refers to a "completed" field, but Todo has no such field. Its fields are id, title, done and due?. The `complete` command sets `done` to true, so "completed" probably means `done`. If it doesn't, the data model would have to change, so I want to confirm before writing the contract.)
governor asks: Todo items have no "completed" field. The field that records completion is `done: boolean`, and the existing `complete <id>` command sets it to true. Should `clear` remove every todo where `done === true`? Or do you want a new `completed` field added to Todo? Also, what should `clear` print? My default would be something like "Cleared N todos." and leaving the other todos and their ids as they are.

